   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT granting retroactive membership in the New York state and local\nemployees' retirement system to Adam Markel",
    "basePrintNo": "S1577",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S1577-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 63,
       "fullName": "Timothy M. Kennedy",
       "imgName": "429_timothy_m._kennedy.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 429,
       "sessionMemberId": 1205,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "KENNEDY"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S1577\n\nSPONSOR: GALLIVAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act granting retroactive membership in the New York state and local\nemployees' retirement system to Adam Markel\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would grant Adam Markel Tier 2 status in the New York State\nPolice and Fire Retirement system upon application.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Authorizes Adam Markel to apply for retroactive membership in\nthe New York State and Local Employees' Retirement System with an effec-\ntive date of September 5, 2006. Once an application is filed with the\nhead of the New York State Police and Fire Retirement system, within one\nyear from the effective date of this act, such service credit will be\ntransferred.\n\nSection 2 states that no contributions made to the New York state Police\nand Fire Retirement System by Adam Markel should be returned or refunded\nto him.\n\nSection 3 states that all past service costs of implementing the\nprovisions of this act shall be borne by the State University of New\nYork at Buffalo.\n\nSection 4: Provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAdam Markel was a part-time employee with the State University of New\nYork at Buffalo from September 5, 2006 until April 14, 2009. However,\nthrough no fault of his own, he did not become a member of the New York\nState and Local Employees' Retirement System during that time.  This\nlegislation would afford Mr. Markel the ability to establish membership\nin the retirement system as of September 5, 2006 thereby correcting this\noversight. It should be noted that all past service costs of implement-\ning the provisions of this act would be borne by the State University of\nNew York at Buffalo.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2018: S.7716/A.9907 Referred to Civil Service and Pensions/Referred to\nGovernmental Employees\n\n2017: S.4253/A.5927 Vetoed by the Governor\n\n2015-16: S.7111/A.9703 Passed Senate/Referred to Governmental Employees\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nSee fiscal note.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
